 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "Who was the most feared ruler in Europe in the 1520s?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Suleiman, the Ottoman sultan. Europeans called him the Magnificent."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did he inherit?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1520",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "His father's huge empire, from the Balkans to Egypt. And he was only in his mid-twenties."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "North of the Danube stood Hungary, the kingdom that guarded central Europe.",
   "scene": "suleiman",
   "date": "1520",
   "place": "Istanbul",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.35,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So where did he strike first?",
   "scene": "first",
   "date": "1521",
   "place": "Belgrade"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "At Belgrade, which fell in 1521. The next year, he took the island of Rhodes from the Knights of Saint John."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And then Hungary itself?",
   "scene": "mohacsmap",
   "date": "1526",
   "place": "Mohács"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Yes. In August 1526, the two armies met at Mohács, on the Danube."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Within about two hours, the Hungarian army was destroyed.",
   "scene": "mohacs",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.35,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.55,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "King Louis the Second drowned in a stream while fleeing. His body was found weeks later.",
   "scene": "louis",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.55,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did that open the road to Vienna?",
   "scene": "viennamap",
   "date": "1529",
   "place": "Vienna"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Three years later, Suleiman marched on Vienna, the Habsburg capital."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "But heavy rain turned the roads to mud, and many of his biggest cannons had to be left behind."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How big were the armies?",
   "scene": "numbers"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Up to a hundred thousand Ottomans at the walls, against about twenty thousand defenders."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So did Vienna fall?",
   "scene": "meldeman",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.35
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. The Ottomans attacked the walls for over two weeks. In mid-October, with rain, cold and supplies running out, Suleiman turned back."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So what did he gain?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1530",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Belgrade, Rhodes, and a Hungarian king who now ruled as his vassal."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: Suleiman the Lawgiver, and Hürrem. Like the video and follow History Sketches.",
   "scene": "lorck",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.35,
     1.2
    ]
   },
   "say": "Next time: Suleiman the Lawgiver, and Hurrem. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: the Lawgiver and Hürrem",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ]
